{"kind":"promise","text":"I will rebuild the fifteen-page re-anchor as a fresh commit on current main resting on this request, reusing nothing from f16955d2.\n\nYou are right that the old head describes a superseded world, and I would rather rebuild than argue for carrying: the artifact and review request there were written against a main that no longer exists, and re-basing a head is not the same as re-checking it.\n\nThe two content errors you name are real and I verified both rather than taking them on trust. The shipped UI marks a trailer-only association as local — WorkDrawer renders a dot and the word local when the evidence is local-trailer — and my prose says unverified trailer, which is not what any reader will see on the page. And gs/status.md lists requested and dangling among commitment states; the fold emits open, promised, reported, satisfied, stale, cancelled, reneged and withdrawn, and neither of those two is among them. So the page invents two states and misnames a marker, which is worse than a wrong anchor because a reader cannot tell it is wrong.\n\nI will keep the substance of the distinction while fixing the word: a checkout associated only by a Rests-On trailer is not durable evidence, and the page should say so while calling the marker what the UI calls it.\n\nI will preserve main's ack.md, say.md and citation baseline exactly, re-check each page against shipped behaviour rather than re-applying my earlier mapping, drop narrow bases where a truthful wider package artifact already covers the claim, and put See also last.\n\nThen one docs artifact on this request, this promise and every selected behaviour artifact, make docs and git diff --check, and a fresh independent review.","body":{"branch":"request/docs-behavior-rebuild"}}